  "turns": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Using the attached complete property and geometry tables, analyze a three-span continuous beam with spans 5, 5 and 5 m along global X. Global +Z is upward. S0 at x=0 is a pin; S1/S2/S3 at x=5/10/15 m are bilateral vertical rollers. Every support rotation about global Y remains free; the beam is continuous without end releases. All spans use M1/B1. Case D is -8 kN/m in global Z over all spans; case W is +6 kN/m in global Z only over the middle span x=5 to 10 m. Define exactly C0=D and C1=D+W. Run first-order linear static Euler-Bernoulli analysis in OpenSees with self-weight disabled. For each of C0 and C1 separately, report all four signed vertical support reactions and all horizontal support reactions, signed uz at x=2.5, 7.5 and 12.5 m, and signed local M2 on both sides of the two internal supports at x=5 and 10 m. Retain signs, including any negative reactions; the rollers restrain both vertical directions. Label every value with its combination, location and unit.\n\nUse the complete attached input tables. Global XYZ is right handed with Z upward; any planar model uses the XZ plane. All nodes listed are connected physical joints. Member local x points from i to j. In 2D local y=global +Y and local z=x cross y. In 3D local y=normalize(reference cross x), local z=x cross y; reference vectors are explicit. N is positive in tension. Signed section N/T/M2/M3 equal minus the i-end resisting action at the start and plus the j-end action at the end; V2/V3 use plus i-end and minus j-end action. Report global nodal displacements and support reactions; rotations follow the right-hand rule. Distributed loads act per actual member length, including inclined members. Use first-order linear elasticity with self-weight, rigid floors, rigid offsets, P-delta and construction stages off. Use only the specified cases and combinations. Compute every request in output-requests.json, retaining its location, side, signed component, unit and case/combination. Interior forces must include applied-load terms. Execute OpenSees and retain version, runnable input, current-model hash, run ID, actual solver log and raw result/case mapping. Report the requested results in the response body as well as structured results; independently check equilibrium. No numerical answer or native execution evidence is supplied.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
      "attachments": [
        "geometry.json",
        "properties.json",
        "loads.json",
        "output-requests.json"
      ],
      "unresolvedFields": [],
      "expectedQuestions": []
    }
  ],
